# Development Guidelines

## Code Organization
- Business logic should be placed in the `Models/` directory
- UI-related code should be kept in XAML files and their code-behind
- Utility functions should go in the `Helpers/` directory
- Data access code should be in the `Data/` directory

## Coding Standards
- Use C# nullable reference types to prevent null reference exceptions
- Follow MVVM pattern where applicable
- Use async/await for I/O operations
- Document public APIs with XML comments
- Handle exceptions appropriately and provide user-friendly error messages

## Building and Testing
- Always build and test in Debug configuration during development
- Use Release configuration for performance testing
- Test on Windows 11 target environment before distribution
- Address all compiler warnings before publishing

## Version Control
- Keep the `.gitignore` file updated
- Don't commit build artifacts in `bin/` and `obj/` directories
- Document significant changes in commit messages

